From 2188690f1434fb6fdfa793f36a106dd66738f4eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:06:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] gdb: k1om (Intel Xeon Phi Knights Corner) target

KNC is x86-64 without MMX/SSE/AVX: the vector unit has 32 512-bit zmm
registers, 8 16-bit mask registers k0-k7 and VXCSR.  Following the k1om
support in Intel's MPSS gdb 7.6.50:

- target description feature org.gnu.gdb.i386.k1om (k0-7, zmm0-31,
  vxcsr) and a k1om tdesc: amd64 core + k1om + segments (+ orig_rax);
- the registers are raw, numbered after the GNU/Linux orig_rax;
- k1om GNU/Linux osabi on top of amd64-linux: SSE-class arguments and
  return values live in the low lanes of zmm0-7, DWARF numbers of the k1om
  GCC (zmm0-15 at 17-32, zmm16-31 at 67-82, k at 118, vxcsr at 126);
- fxsave without SSE registers, and the vector unit block of the KNC
  NT_X86_XSTATE layout (fxsave area, xsave header, zmm, k, vxcsr), also
  for core files;
- report return values as unavailable and refuse to pass arguments in
  vector registers whose value is not available.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
